From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:23:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix SCS work across radio stop and SER

The SCS work is one work for the whole device, but since d258f4e3e1ca
("wifi: mt76: mt7996: switch to single multi-radio wiphy") the radio
stop path runs for one radio at a time. Stopping one radio therefore
cancels the SCS feed of the radios that still run. The L1 SER path
leaves the work running, so SCS commands can go out during the DMA
recovery, and device removal never cancels the work.

The work now stops by itself when no radio runs with SCS enabled, is
cancelled on removal and for the length of an L1 SER, and resumes
after the SER. A poll that runs during a reset skips its firmware
command but stays queued, so the feed resumes after a full reset too.
Enabling SCS on a radio that does not run no longer queues the work,
because the radio start queues it.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/init.c |    4 ++++
 mt7996/mac.c  |    7 +++++++
 mt7996/main.c |    1 -
 mt7996/mcu.c  |   12 ++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -1980,6 +1980,10 @@ void mt7996_unregister_device(struct mt7
 	cancel_work_sync(&dev->rc_work);
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&phy->mt76->mac_work);
+	/* a debugfs write can queue the work until mac80211 removes
+	 * debugfs, which happens after this point
+	 */
+	disable_delayed_work_sync(&dev->scs_work);
 	mt7996_unregister_phy(mt7996_phy3(dev));
 	mt7996_unregister_phy(mt7996_phy2(dev));
 	mt7996_unregister_thermal(&dev->phy);
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2495,6 +2495,7 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_s
 		set_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->mt76->state);
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&phy->mt76->mac_work);
 	}
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dev->scs_work);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
@@ -2623,6 +2624,12 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_s
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
 		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(hw, &phy->mt76->mac_work,
 					     MT7996_WATCHDOG_TIME);
+
+	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy) {
+		if (test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &phy->mt76->state) &&
+		    phy->scs_ctrl.scs_enable)
+			ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(hw, &dev->scs_work, HZ);
+	}
 	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,"==== %s L1 SER recovery completed ====",
 		 wiphy_name(dev->mt76.hw->wiphy));
 }
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -123,7 +123,6 @@ static void mt7996_stop_phy(struct mt799
 	dev = phy->dev;
 
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&phy->mt76->mac_work);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dev->scs_work);
 	wiphy_delayed_work_cancel(phy->mt76->hw->wiphy,
 				  &phy->mt76->assoc_chan_work);
 
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -6447,10 +6447,17 @@ void mt7996_mcu_scs_sta_poll(struct work
 		    !phy->scs_ctrl.scs_enable)
 			continue;
 
+		/* the MCU takes no commands during recovery, but the work
+		 * stays queued so that the feed resumes after it
+		 */
+		scs_enable_flag = true;
+		if (test_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state) ||
+		    test_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->mt76->state))
+			continue;
+
 		ieee80211_iterate_stations_atomic(phy->mt76->hw,
 						  mt7996_sta_rssi_work, phy);
 
-		scs_enable_flag = true;
 		if (mt7996_mcu_set_scs_stats(phy))
 			dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "Failed to send scs mcu cmd\n");
 		phy->scs_ctrl.sta_min_rssi = 0;
@@ -6482,7 +6489,8 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_scs(struct mt7996_phy
 
 	phy->scs_ctrl.scs_enable = enable;
 
-	if (enable == SCS_ENABLE)
+	if (enable == SCS_ENABLE &&
+	    test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &phy->mt76->state))
 		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &dev->scs_work, HZ);
 
 	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(&phy->dev->mt76, MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(SCS),
